# Checked in deliberately -- none of this is secret (it mirrors eas.json's
# build.production/preview env blocks) and it's the safety net that keeps a
# release build correct even when it's produced outside EAS (e.g. running
# `gradlew assembleRelease` directly against a locally-generated android/
# project, which never reads eas.json -- see the incident where a locally
# built release APK silently baked in .env.local's http://localhost:3000
# because that file is loaded for every build type, dev and release alike).
